@startuml mailbox-delivery
!theme plain
title Mailbox delivery: key-class verdicts, narrowing guard, host admission and own-key outbound signing
' Updated: accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13)

database "Carrier\n(Matrix / XMPP)" as MX
participant "Carrier provider\n(child process)" as MP
participant "Bridge core\n(trust gate)" as BR
participant "Trust\n(keys, grants, revocation)" as T
participant "Decision guard\n(small local model)" as DG
database "Mailbox\n(bodies + verification records)" as MB
participant "Session host\n(admission, dispatcher)" as SH
participant "Agent\n(own OS account)" as A
participant "Key keeper" as KK

== inbound ==
MX -> MP: event addressed to the session
MP -> MP: persist (fsync); advance cursor
MP -> BR: envelope bytes
BR -> T: exact-byte signature; admitted key class; action/target grant;\nfreshness, replay and current binding (ADM §3; TRU §6)
alt unsigned
  T --> BR: quarantine
  BR -> MB: persist held body
  BR -> SH: enqueue metadata-only doorbell
  SH -> SH: admit(); durable inbox; dispatch only with open fence
  SH -> A: doorbell only; body fetched as tool output
else invalid signature, unknown key or other gate failure
  T --> BR: reject
  BR -> MB: refusal receipt and audit; no delivery
else enrolled operator key or admitted peer key
  T --> BR: operator key enrolled for binding: authoritative for granted typed action;\npeer key: data, no effect authority
  BR -> DG: admitted body + verification record + grant specification
  DG -> MB: record narrowing decision and fingerprint
  alt guard unavailable or no-go
    BR -> MB: refuse delivery; guard cannot elevate a verdict
  else guard go
    alt enrolled operator key and granted typed action
      BR -> SH: enqueue authoritative typed action
      SH -> SH: admit() again at every mutation;\nre-admit at dispatch (ADM §4)
      SH -> A: user turn only if session.input admission passes
    else peer key
      BR -> SH: enqueue data + verification record
      SH -> SH: admit() again; no approval or control authority
      SH -> A: UNTRUSTED PEER EVENTS frame
    end
  end
end

== fetch held body ==
A -> MB: inbox read (tool; binding grant; session token)
MB --> A: body + verification record as tool output

== outbound ==
A -> KK: sign exact outbound bytes under own UID (TRU §2)
KK -> KK: active generation-bound registration; own key only
KK --> A: signature
A -> BR: post signed item (binding grant; rate-limited; audited)
BR -> BR: verify exact signed bytes and audience projection;\nno rewriting of signed content
BR -> MP: admitted signed output
MP -> MX: post; ordinary text with signature metadata
@enduml
